// Concrete (naive but exact) incident-edge neighborhood backend +
// paper-style case (2)/(3) merge algebra, label-sliced by a sparse label λ.
//
// This is NOT the complete BOJ solver. It is the concrete implementation of the
// two pieces previously missing from the sparse-label runtime skeleton:
//   1) real N_v-like backend API over incident tree-edge ground sets,
//   2) paper-style totalcnt / diagcnt* / totalmarks / diagmarks* merge algebra.
//
// The implementation is exact but deliberately naive:
//  - no biased disjoint sets,
//  - no top-tree dynamic engine,
//  - no attempt at the paper's asymptotic performance.
//
// It is meant to be a concrete drop-in backend/algebra layer for integration.

